1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,400
Section 1

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:02,344
MARTHA:

3
00:00:02,344 --> 00:00:03,047
Hi Alex.

4
00:00:03,047 --> 00:00:04,367
It's Martha Clines here.

5
00:00:04,367 --> 00:00:06,910
James White gave me your number.

6
00:00:06,910 --> 00:00:10,300
I hope you don't mind me calling you.

7
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:10,700
ALEX:

8
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:11,900
Of course not.

9
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:13,500
How are you, Martha?

10
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:13,933
MARTHA:

11
00:00:13,933 --> 00:00:14,800
Good thanks.

12
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:18,700
I'm ringing because I need a bit of advice.

13
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:19,140
ALEX:

14
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:20,020
Oh yeah.

15
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:20,900
What about?

16
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:21,309
MARTHA:

17
00:00:21,309 --> 00:00:25,397
The training you did at JPNW a few years ago.

18
00:00:25,397 --> 00:00:27,850
I'm applying for the same thing.

19
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:28,233
ALEX:

20
00:00:28,233 --> 00:00:29,000
Oh right.

21
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,300
Yes, I did mine in 2014.

22
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:33,217
Best thing I ever did.

23
00:00:33,217 --> 00:00:34,750
I'm still working there.

24
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:35,325
MARTHA:

25
00:00:35,325 --> 00:00:35,900
Really?

26
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:38,200
What are you doing?

27
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:38,509
ALEX:

28
00:00:38,509 --> 00:00:42,832
Well, now I work in the customer services department but I did my initial

29
00:00:42,832 --> 00:00:43,759
training in Finance.

30
00:00:43,759 --> 00:00:48,082
I stayed there for the first two years and then moved to where I

31
00:00:48,082 --> 00:00:48,700
am now.

32
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:49,133
MARTHA:

33
00:00:49,133 --> 00:00:52,167
That's the same department I'm applying for.

34
00:00:52,167 --> 00:00:53,900
Did you enjoy it?

35
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:54,199
ALEX:

36
00:00:54,199 --> 00:00:56,290
I was pretty nervous to begin with.

37
00:00:56,290 --> 00:01:00,472
I didn't do well in my exams at school and I was really worried

38
00:01:00,472 --> 00:01:01,668
because I failed Maths.

39
00:01:01,668 --> 00:01:05,850
But it didn't actually matter because I did lots of courses on the job.

40
00:01:05,850 --> 00:01:06,175
MARTHA:

41
00:01:06,175 --> 00:01:10,075
Did you get a diploma at the end of your trainee period?

42
00:01:10,075 --> 00:01:13,000
I'm hoping to do the one in business skills.

43
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:13,318
ALEX:

44
00:01:13,318 --> 00:01:13,635
Yes.

45
00:01:13,635 --> 00:01:14,588
That sounds good.

46
00:01:14,588 --> 00:01:19,032
I took the one on IT skills but I wish I'd done that one

47
00:01:19,032 --> 00:01:19,350
instead.

48
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:19,786
MARTHA:

49
00:01:19,786 --> 00:01:20,222
OK,

50
00:01:20,222 --> 00:01:21,967
that's good to know.

51
00:01:21,967 --> 00:01:24,147
What about the other trainees?

52
00:01:24,147 --> 00:01:27,200
How did you get on with them?

53
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:27,535
ALEX:

54
00:01:27,535 --> 00:01:31,560
There were about 20 of us who started at the same time

55
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:35,250
and we were all around the same age - I was 18

56
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:38,269
and there was only one person younger than me,

57
00:01:38,269 --> 00:01:39,275
who was 17.

58
00:01:39,275 --> 00:01:41,623
The rest were between 18 and 20.

59
00:01:41,623 --> 00:01:43,300
I made some good friends.

60
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:43,668
MARTHA:

61
00:01:43,668 --> 00:01:47,718
I've heard lots of good things about the training at JPNW.

62
00:01:47,718 --> 00:01:51,400
It seems like there are a lot of opportunities there.

63
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:51,789
ALEX:

64
00:01:51,789 --> 00:01:52,567
Yeah, definitely.

65
00:01:52,567 --> 00:01:58,011
Because of its size you can work in loads of different areas within the

66
00:01:58,011 --> 00:01:58,400
organisation.

67
00:01:58,400 --> 00:01:58,840
MARTHA:

68
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:00,160
What about pay?

69
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:05,000
I know you get a lower minimum wage than regular employees.

70
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:05,286
ALEX:

71
00:02:05,286 --> 00:02:06,719
That's right - which isn't great.

72
00:02:06,719 --> 00:02:10,157
But you get the same number of days' holiday as everyone else.

73
00:02:10,157 --> 00:02:14,168
And the pay goes up massively if they offer you a job at the

74
00:02:14,168 --> 00:02:15,600
end of the training period.

75
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:15,950
MARTHA:

76
00:02:15,950 --> 00:02:16,300
Yeah,

77
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:20,850
but I'm not doing it for the money - it's the experience I think

78
00:02:20,850 --> 00:02:22,250
will be really useful.

79
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:26,800
Everyone says by the end of the year you gain so much confidence.

80
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:27,147
ALEX:

81
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:27,841
You're right.

82
00:02:27,841 --> 00:02:30,271
That's the most useful part about it.

83
00:02:30,271 --> 00:02:32,353
There's a lot of variety too.

84
00:02:32,353 --> 00:02:35,129
You're given lots of different things to do.

85
00:02:35,129 --> 00:02:38,600
I enjoyed it all - I didn't even mind the studying.

86
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:38,905
MARTHA:

87
00:02:38,905 --> 00:02:41,650
Do you have to spend any time in college?

88
00:02:41,650 --> 00:02:41,995
ALEX:

89
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:43,718
Yes, one day each month.

90
00:02:43,718 --> 00:02:48,200
So you get lots of support from both your tutor and your manager.

91
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:48,631
MARTHA:

92
00:02:48,631 --> 00:02:49,492
That's good.

93
00:02:49,492 --> 00:02:53,800
And the company is easy to get to, isn't it?

94
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:54,177
ALEX:

95
00:02:54,177 --> 00:02:59,450
Yes, it's very close to the train station so the location's a real advantage.

96
00:02:59,450 --> 00:02:59,765
ALEX:

97
00:02:59,765 --> 00:03:02,600
Have you got a date for your interview yet?

98
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:03,033
MARTHA:

99
00:03:03,033 --> 00:03:06,500
Yes, it's on the 23rd of this month.

100
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:06,877
ALEX:

101
00:03:06,877 --> 00:03:11,020
So long as you're well prepared there's nothing to worry about.

102
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:12,150
Everyone's very friendly.

103
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:12,554
MARTHA:

104
00:03:12,554 --> 00:03:15,785
I am not sure what I should wear.

105
00:03:15,785 --> 00:03:17,400
What do you think?

106
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:17,800
ALEX:

107
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:20,600
Nothing too casual - like jeans, for example.

108
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:25,800
If you've got a nice jacket, wear that with a skirt or trousers.

109
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,517
MARTHA:

110
00:03:26,517 --> 00:03:27,233
OK.

111
00:03:27,233 --> 00:03:27,950
Thanks.

112
00:03:27,950 --> 00:03:30,100
Any other tips?

113
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:30,411
ALEX:

114
00:03:30,411 --> 00:03:34,453
Erm, well I know it's really obvious but arrive in plenty of time.

115
00:03:34,453 --> 00:03:36,319
They hate people who are late.

116
00:03:36,319 --> 00:03:40,050
So make sure you know exactly where you have to get to.

117
00:03:40,050 --> 00:03:45,094
And one other useful piece of advice my manager told me before I had

118
00:03:45,094 --> 00:03:47,976
the interview for this job - is to smile.

119
00:03:47,976 --> 00:03:49,778
Even if you feel terrified.

120
00:03:49,778 --> 00:03:52,300
It makes people respond better to you.

121
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:52,740
MARTHA:

122
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:56,700
I'll have to practise doing that in the mirror!

123
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:57,075
ALEX:

124
00:03:57,075 --> 00:03:58,575
Yeah - well, good luck.

125
00:03:58,575 --> 00:04:01,950
Let me know if you need any more information.

126
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:02,638
MARTHA:

127
00:04:02,638 --> 00:04:04,700
Thanks very much.
